-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",46,{
[1441]="70052941\n1\tCollect boar meat in Laerlad (total: 12)\tBoars can be found in Laerlad in the Vales of Anduin. You should collect boar meat for the Woodfolk of Blómgard.\n2\tBring the boar meat to Evorik\tEvorik can be found in Blómgard. You should talk to Evorik.\n",
[1442]="7005224B\n1\tRadagast has many tasks that need completing in the Vales of Anduin. You should assist Radagast in the Vales of Anduin.\t\n2\tComplete Rhosgobel: Radagast's Garden\030Complete Rhosgobel: The Daily Egg\030Complete Rhosgobel: Cleaning the Anduin\030Complete Rhosgobel: Cleaning the Tributaries\030Complete Rhosgobel: Calming the Farm\030Complete Rhosgobel: Calming the Wilds\tRadagast has many tasks that need completing in the Vales of Anduin. You should assist Radagast in the Vales of Anduin.\n3\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should talk to Radagast.\n",
[1443]="700442A7\n1\tSpeak with Ingold\tIngold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Ingold and assist him with protecting the Rammas.\n2\tComplete Quest: Retaking the Northern Rammas\tIngold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Ingold and assist him with protecting the Rammas.\n3\tSpeak with Londir\tLondir can be found in Minas Tirith. Speak with Londir.\n",
[1444]="70044D75\n1\tSpeak with Rathon\tRathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon and assist him with protecting the Cisterns.\n2\tComplete Quest: Finding a Breach in the Darkness\tRathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon and assist him with protecting the Cisterns.\n3\tSpeak with Heledon\tHeledon can be found in Minas Tirith. Speak with Heledon.\n",
[1445]="7006EC24\n1\tCollect fresh herbs (total: 4)\030Collect juicy lemons (total: 4)\030Collect handfuls of olives (total: 4)\tSâghlem has asked you to collect three ingredients that grow on the slopes that rise above Furtherholm.\n2\tBring the ingredients to Sâghlem\tYou have collected the ingredients for which Sâghlem asked. You should bring them to him in the kitchen of The Cracked Flagon in Furtherholm.\n",
[1446]="70047729\n1\tQuests for the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien can be found at the Camp of the Host and within Henneth Annûn.\t\n2\tComplete quests for the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien (total: 4)\tYou should complete quests for the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien. Quests for the benefit of the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien can be found at the Camp of the Host and within Henneth Annûn.\n",
[1447]="70059439\n1\tPick up wood scraps (total: 12)\tWood scraps can be found throughout Trestlebridge. You should help out and pick up the wood scraps.\n2\tDeliver the wood scraps to the lumber pile\tA lumber pile can be found in Trestlebridge. You should deliver the wood scraps to the lumber pile.\n3\tTalk to Nessa Larch\tNessa Larch can be found in Trestlebridge. You should talk to Nessa Larch.\n",
[1448]="700442B8\n1\tSpeak with Turgon\tTurgon can be found at the southern gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Turgon and assist him with clearing the port of the Harlond.\n2\tComplete Quest: Dredging a Path for Aragorn\tTurgon can be found at the southern gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Turgon and assist him with clearing the port of the Harlond.\n3\tSpeak with Narnaith\tNarnaith can be found in Minas Tirith. Speak with Narnaith.\n",
[1449]="70071B32\n1\tReturn to Mírthar with the healing concoction\tLóburdith has helped you complete the healing concoction needed to save Mírthar. Hurry back and give him the medicine.\n2\tInspect Mírthar\tMírthar's body appears lifeless when you arrived with the healing concoction. Inspect him to learn any more that you can.\n3\tBring Mírthar's scholar's mark to Serâna\tYou found Mírthar's scholar's mark when inspecting him. Bring it to the scholar Serâna in Sul Madásh, she would want to know of his fate.\n",
[1450]="70060582\n1\tTalk to Erlys\tErlys has decided to free Cariad from Tornhad with your aid and Igrain's. You should talk to her in the Cuan-lûth Refuge when you're ready.\n2\tTalk to Erlys\tErlys would like to speak with you before you depart the Cuan-lûth Refuge.\n",
[1451]="70019D3D\n1\tFind the flet-runner by the entrance to the Crafting Hall\tThe flet-runner can be found on a flet with a mailbox high above Telain Galadhrim, near the entrance to the Crafting Hall. Celechest has challenged you to quickly make your way to a certain flet-runner. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to the flet-runner by the Crafting Hall\tThe flet-runner by the entrance to the Crafting Hall on Telain Galadhrim is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[1452]="70072CAD\n1\tFind and pet ten of the cats to be found in Zajâna.\t\n2\tReturn to Jarôba in Zajâna\tReturn to Jarôba in Zajâna with the names and locations of the cats you have found.\n",
[1453]="70052B15\n1\tDeliver Grimbeorn's message to Hárskor in Hultvís\tThe settlement of Hultvís can be found far to the south of the Beorning-lands in Woodsedge. Grimbeorn has asked you to seek one of his kin, Hárskor, and aid the chieftain of the Woodmen, Ríkmar.\n2\tTalk to Ríkmar in Hultvís\tRíkmar, chieftain of the Woodmen, can be found in the settlement of Hultvís in Woodsedge. Grimbeorn sent his kinsman, Hárskor, to Woodsedge bearing much-needed supplies for the Woodmen of the Vales of Anduin. However, Hárskor has not returned and you have found no sign of his passing in Hultvís.\n",
[1454]="7002EF7D\n1\tSeek clues at Éomer's Vengeance\tÉomer's Vengeance lies to the west of Thornhope. Thane Béortnoth bade you seek answers to the mystery of what occured at Éomer's Vengeance.\n2\tFind the source of the camp-fire's smoke\tA thin pillar of campfire smoke can be seen to the west. You should find the camp-fire, for perhaps the friends or foes you find will have answers about what took place here.\n3\tTalk to a fisherman\tThe men at this fishing-encampment at the edge of the Entwash and Fangorn appear friendly. You should speak to a fisherman at the camp.\n",
[1455]="7001AF95\n1\tDefeat angry bears (total: 8)\030Defeat large barrow-crawlers (total: 24)\tThe bears and the disease-bearing crawlers can be found on the border of the southern Barrow-downs and Old Forest. Bob Redthistle wants to destroy the diseased bears before they spread their plague throughout the Old Forest.\n2\tTalk to Bob Redthistle at the Dead Man's Perch\tBob Redthistle can be found at the Dead Man's Perch. You should return to Bob Redthistle and tell him that the grim work he required is complete.\n",
[1456]="70058C91\n1\tFind some sign of Glóin's scouts near the gates of Mount Gundabad\tDarfin, Zhúdo, Rádek, and Sigvith can be found near the gates of Mount Gundabad. Glóin's scouts have not returned from a mission to the gates of Mount Gundabad. You should search for them.\n2\tTalk to Zhúdo near Mount Gundabad\tZhúdo can be found near Mount Gundabad. You have found only one of Glóin's scouts, Zhúdo. You should talk to Zhúdo and learn what has happened.\n3\tFind and aid Darfin\030Find and aid Rádek\030Find and aid Sigvith\tDarfin, Rádek, and Sigvith can be found within the encampments of Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh at the gates of Mount Gundabad. Zhúdo has asked you to recall Darfin, Rádek, and Sigvith from their missions at the Orc encampments outside Mount Gundabad.\n4\tTalk to Zhúdo near Mount Gundabad\tZhúdo can be found near Mount Gundabad. You have recalled the other scouts sent to Gundabad. You should return to Zhúdo.\n",
[1457]="70042F60\n1\tDefeat Orc raft-builders (total: 8)\030Burn Orkish bridge-rafts (total: 8)\tOrc raft-builders and their designs can be found along the Anduin in southern Osgiliath. Golthor has asked you to sabotage Orkish bridge-rafts and slay their crafters.\n2\tTalk to Golthor\tGolthor can be found in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath. You have dealt a harsh blow to the Orcs along the Anduin and should now return to Golthor.\n",
[1458]="70049556\n1\tStout-axe expeditions can be found throughout Dor Amarth. Spakorth has asked you to seek the remaining Stout-axe expeditions in Dor Amarth. These expeditions can be found among the rocks and crevices to the south of the road to Lûghash. You should tell any Stout-axes you encounter to return to Lûghash.\t\n2\tTalk to Spakorth at Lûghash\tSpakorth can be found outside the lower gates to Lûghash in Dor Amarth. You have recalled all the Stout-axes you could find. You should meet with Spakorth outside Lûghash.\n",
[1459]="7002F92B\n1\tEnter the cave where Zúrsnaga is hiding\tThe Uruk-hideout is south-west of Caddabrand's camp, beyond the entrance to the wolf-den. Caddabrand has tracked the Uruk, Zúrsnaga, to a cave south-west of the wolf den.\n2\tFind and defeat Zúrsnaga the Uruk\tThe Uruk-hideout is south-west of Caddabrand's camp, beyond the entrance to the wolf-den. Zúrsnaga lies hidden within the caves. Caddabrand has asked you to find and defeat the Uruk, Zúrsnaga.\n3\tReturn to Caddabrand with news of Zúrsnaga's demise\tCaddabrand's camp lies east of the Uruk-hai hideout and the wolf-den. Caddabrand will be eager to hear the news that Zúrsnaga has been defeated.\n",
[1460]="7002F986\n1\tTalk to Léofcetel\tLéofcetel can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving. Captain Garmund wishes to have Léofcetel rejoin his men and to set aside their past differences.\n2\tTalk to Reeve Athelward at the Mead Hall\tReeve Athelward resides within his Mead Hall, at the eastern edge of Cliving. Reeve Athelward has summoned you before him to discuss the matters of Garmund and Léofcetel.\n3\tInform Léofcetel of his promotion to Captain of the Guard\tLéofcetel can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving. Reeve Athelward has judged Léofcetel worthy of the title of Captain of the Guard, receiving the role from his rival Garmund.\n4\tInform Garmund of his new role as Athelward's personal guardian\tGarmund can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving. Athelward has judged Garmund to be a valiant protector and has granted him the duty of becoming the Reeve's personal safe-guard.\n",
[1461]="7000E8FE\n1\tCollect Beakbreaker Ale from the Comb and Wattle\tThe Comb and Wattle Inn is in the village of Combe in Bree-land. You should travel to Combe and collect some Beakbreaker Ale from the inn there.\n2\tBring the Beakbreaker Ale to Óli\tÓli is at Hrimbarg in the Misty Mountains, far to the east of Bree-land. Óli has asked you to bring him a pint of \"Beakbreaker Ale\" from The Comb and Wattle Inn.\n",
[1462]="700271E5\n1\tSecure the main gate\tBreach and secure the main gate of Dol Dínen.\n2\tSecure the western gate\030Secure the eastern gate\tBreach either the western or eastern gate of Dol Dínen.\n3\tSecure the central gate\tWith a path cleared through one of the gates, the central gate now bars your way from reaching the goblin-scouts.\n4\tSecure the entrance of Graug's encampment\tSecure the entrance of the Graug's encampment at the top of the hill looking down upon the central gate.\n5\tSecure the area.\030Destroy catapults (total: 2)\tSeek out and destroy the catapults that lie outside Graug's tent. This will allow the Rangers below to secure the camp below.\n6\tDefeat Graug and secure the knowledge of Esteldín's location\tThe courtyard has fallen. Now all that remains is to defeat Graug and destroy any remnants of the information that he has gathered. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[1463]="70029FCB\n1\tComplete 'Attack at Dawn' in a raid group\tLate in the night, a party of goblin-scouts discovered the location of the Ranger-refuge known as Esteldín. The goblins have fled to Dol Dínen, where you must dispatch them before they can bring reinforcements.\n",
[1464]="7007177B\n1\tBefore departing for Zajâna, Rhadrog asks you to deal with Ombátha, who will continue to pose a threat to An Shêru. Whether you choose to do so alone or with allies, you should enter the interior of Kôth Rau and battle Ombátha and whatever other threats you discover within.\t\n2\tTalk to Nabatínu\tYou have defeated the leadership of the Ordâkhai and the Utûgi at Kôth Rau. You should report your success to Nabatínu at Gadim-ûn.\n",
[1465]="7004BEB5\n1\tDefeat foes at Fushaum Bal South (total: 6)\tFushaum Bal is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat those who dwell at Fushaum Bal South.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many foes at Fushaum Bal South.\n",
[1466]="7004BEB7\n1\tDefeat foes at Fushaum Bal North (total: 6)\tFushaum Bal North is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat those who dwell at Fushaum Bal North.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many foes at Fushaum Bal North.\n",
[1467]="7001A4AB\n1\tDefeat Laehendiel at the Dreadweaver's Lair\030Defeat spiders in the Dourstocks (total: 5)\tSpiders may be found throughout the Dourstocks. Laehendiel may be found at the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-east from Echad Mothelen. Lavanferon has asked you to defeat many spiders and their mistress, Laehendiel.\n2\tTalk to Lavanferon at Echad Mothelen\tLavanferon is at Echad Mothelen, north-west from the Dreadweaver's Lair. You should return to Lavanferon with tidings of your success.\n",
[1468]="70007017\n1\tBring the aurochs mantles back to Gondranc\030Collect aurochs-mantles (total: 4)\tAurochs graze the plains and hills of Rhunenlad and eastern Nan Amlug. Gondranc learned from Asikko's book that the Earth-kin use the fur mantles which grow upon the shoulders of the aurochs to pad their armour. He has asked you to hunt aurochs and bring him these mantles.\n",
[1469]="70062AA8\n1\tCollect boar-meat from Mosshide boars (total: 10)\tMosshide boars dwell near the Old South Road, and will prove a good source of the boar-steaks for which Bevan asked.\n2\tBring the boar-meat to Bevan at the north gate of Mossward\tBevan is at the north gate of Mossward, waiting for you to return with boar-meat.\n",
[1470]="700529A7\n1\tDestroy sorrowful relics (total: 8)\tAudvak believes that destroying sorrowful relics may help lift the darkness that has settled upon Avabárg.\n",
[1471]="700529A5\n1\tDefeat the Spirit of Gloom\tThe gloom of which Audvak spoke was not merely metaphorical, and has taken ethereal forms that must be defeated.\n",
[1472]="7005299E\n1\tDefeat silent glooms (total: 12)\030Defeat shadow wolves (total: 6)\tThe gloom of which Audvak spoke was not merely metaphorical, and has taken ethereal forms that must be defeated.\n",
})
